<Project>

  <!--
    Emit XML documentation files for every project under src/.

    Without this, `dotnet pack` produces packages that contain only the .dll and
    no AiDotNet.xml, so IntelliSense in Visual Studio / Rider shows NO doc tooltips
    for any public member — even though the source is richly commented. Enabling
    GenerateDocumentationFile makes the build emit <Assembly>.xml, which the .NET
    SDK pack target then includes in the package lib/ folder alongside the .dll.

    The XML-doc warning family (CS1591 and 19 related codes) is NOT suppressed with <NoWarn>
    any more: NoWarn overrides every analyzer-config severity, which made it impossible to hold
    part of the codebase to a documentation standard while the rest catches up (issue #2393).
    XmlDocDiagnostics.globalconfig (included below) sets them to "none" for every file, which
    is the old behaviour and also covers source-generator output; a path section in the
    repository .editorconfig overrides that to "error" for the documented user-facing facade
    (AiModelBuilder, AiModelResult, the Serving extensions and the interfaces they expose).
    The compiler still emits <Assembly>.xml for every well-formed comment either way.
  -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <GenerateDocumentationFile>true</GenerateDocumentationFile>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <GlobalAnalyzerConfigFiles Include="$(MSBuildThisFileDirectory)XmlDocDiagnostics.globalconfig" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
